SLUG: terms.html
TITLE: Terms of Service | Akash Movers, Kanpur
DESC: The terms covering quotes, bookings, what we need from you, items we cannot carry, liability and claims, storage, payment and complaints.
HEADING: Terms of service
LEAD: The terms that apply to quotes and bookings. The figures for your particular move — deposit, notice, cover and payment — are set out in your written quotation.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Terms|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow flow">

        <!-- The developer-facing "template, not ready to publish" banner that
             used to sit here has gone. It was addressed to whoever was
             building the site, and it was being shown to customers on a live
             page linked from every footer.

             The six [TO BE SUPPLIED] blanks under it have NOT been filled
             with invented policy. Each one now states the thing this site
             consistently says everywhere else — that the figures for a
             particular job are confirmed in writing with the quotation —
             which is a description of the process, not a policy made up by a
             website. A cancellation fee or a liability cap invented here
             would be unenforceable at best and misleading at worst.

             WHAT STILL NEEDS THE OWNER: the actual deposit, notice period,
             cancellation scale, cover options, claim window, payment terms
             and complaint acknowledgement time, plus a legal review. Until
             those exist as real policy they belong in the quotation, where
             they are agreed per job, and not as numbers on a web page. -->

        <p class="lead">
          These terms apply to every quotation and booking. They are
          deliberately short, and they point to your written quotation for
          anything that varies by job — because it does vary by job, and a
          figure printed here would not be the one that applies to you.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who these terms are between</h2>
        <p>
          These terms apply between
          <strong data-config="business.name">the company</strong> and the
          customer requesting or booking moving services. Submitting an
          enquiry does not create a booking; a booking exists once we have
          confirmed it in writing.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Quotes and estimates</h2>
        <p>
          A quote is based on the inventory and access described during the
          survey. It is valid for the period stated on the quote itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          If, on the day, the goods or the access differ materially from what
          was described — significantly more items, a floor or lift situation
          not disclosed, or a carry distance substantially longer than agreed
          — we will set out the revised cost and obtain your approval before
          continuing. We will not complete the work and present a different
          figure afterwards.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Booking, rescheduling and cancellation</h2>
        <p>
          What is payable to confirm a booking, how much notice is needed to
          reschedule, and the terms that apply if you cancel are set out in
          your written quotation and agreed before the booking is confirmed.
          Ask for them in writing if they are not clear to you — they should
          be on the quotation before you commit to anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          If we have to reschedule, we will tell you as soon as we know and
          agree a new date with you.
        </p>

        <h2>4. What we need from you</h2>
        <p>To do the job properly we need you to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Describe the inventory and the access accurately at survey</li>
          <li>Obtain any building or society permission needed for the move</li>
          <li>Be present, or have an authorised adult present, at both addresses</li>
          <li>Carry jewellery, cash, documents and other high-value small items yourself</li>
          <li>Empty and disconnect gas cylinders, and defrost and drain appliances, before the day</li>
          <li>Check the inventory against the goods at delivery and note anything wrong on the sheet before the crew leaves</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Items we cannot carry</h2>
        <p>
          We do not transport cash, jewellery, government documents,
          firearms, hazardous or flammable goods, loaded gas cylinders,
          perishable food, illegal items, or live animals. Pets should travel
          with you. Plants can be carried on local moves but travel poorly
          over long distances, and we will tell you so rather than take the
          booking.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Liability and claims</h2>
        <p>
          Transit cover is an option, not an automatic inclusion. The cover
          available for your consignment, what it covers, any limit, the
          window for reporting damage or loss, and what is excluded are
          confirmed in writing with your quotation before the move.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Nothing on this website is a promise of insurance or
          compensation.</strong> If cover matters to you, ask for the terms in
          writing with your quote and read them before you book. Report any
          damage to your coordinator at delivery and note it on the delivery
          sheet while the crew is still on site — that is what makes a claim
          straightforward afterwards.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Storage</h2>
        <p>
          Where goods are held in storage, they are inventoried in and out and
          charged by duration, separately from the move. The applicable rate,
          the billing period, the notice needed to release goods and what
          happens if charges fall into arrears are confirmed in writing before
          anything enters storage.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Payment</h2>
        <p>
          Accepted payment methods, when payment falls due relative to loading
          and delivery, and whether any part is payable in advance are set out
          in your written quotation. We do not ask for payment terms to be
          agreed on the day.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          Raise any problem with your coordinator first — most things are
          fixed fastest while the crew is still on site. If it is not
          resolved, contact us through the
          <a href="/contact.html">contact page</a>, by phone or on WhatsApp,
          and ask for it to be escalated to the proprietor. Put the move
          reference and the date in your message so the job can be found
          quickly.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at
          <strong data-config="business.primaryCity">Kanpur</strong> have
          jurisdiction.
        </p>

        <p class="form-note mt-7">
          Last updated <time data-updated-date>17 October 2026</time>.
          These terms have not been reviewed by a lawyer. If anything here
          conflicts with the written quotation you were given, the quotation
          is the document that governs your booking.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
